1
00:00:56,891 --> 00:00:57,725
Wait.

2
00:00:59,226 --> 00:01:00,644
Hey, hold on.

3
00:01:02,229 --> 00:01:03,564
The boarding gates are that way.

4
00:01:20,414 --> 00:01:21,582
Let's do it.

5
00:01:22,541 --> 00:01:24,585
What? Do what?

6
00:01:24,668 --> 00:01:25,836
Let's do it together.

7
00:01:27,004 --> 00:01:29,381
The Table: K-Chef 2026.

8
00:01:38,057 --> 00:01:40,684
The days when chefs
stayed in the kitchen are over.

9
00:01:41,185 --> 00:01:44,271
Of course, that doesn't mean
we can leave the kitchen behind.

10
00:01:45,689 --> 00:01:48,442
The point is, R&D and business

11
00:01:48,526 --> 00:01:53,113
need to be balanced on the same scale.

12
00:01:53,781 --> 00:01:56,367
Korean dining can't grow
without economies of scale.

13
00:01:57,201 --> 00:01:58,452
That's right.

14
00:01:58,536 --> 00:02:01,956
As you said, I also think
that without a strong business foundation,

15
00:02:02,039 --> 00:02:06,460
this industry will remain something
only a few gourmets can enjoy.

16
00:02:07,086 --> 00:02:09,964
K-food has gained worldwide popularity,

17
00:02:10,047 --> 00:02:13,926
but mainly through casual street food.

18
00:02:14,009 --> 00:02:17,847
Some are pessimistic about its future
and say it'll soon hit a wall.

19
00:02:17,930 --> 00:02:18,931
That's true.

20
00:02:19,014 --> 00:02:20,307
Considering that reality,

21
00:02:20,391 --> 00:02:24,061
what do you think the restaurant industry
should strive for?

22
00:02:26,272 --> 00:02:28,649
I'd like to know your personal opinion.

23
00:02:32,862 --> 00:02:33,988
That's a tough one.

24
00:02:36,448 --> 00:02:37,658
Realistically speaking,

25
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:40,744
what should we strive for?

26
00:02:47,418 --> 00:02:52,339
I hear Pyeongyeon Group
is planning a very interesting show

27
00:02:52,423 --> 00:02:55,050
called The Table: K-Chef 2026.

28
00:02:55,843 --> 00:02:58,679
The aim is to find
the best Korean chef in the world,

29
00:02:58,762 --> 00:03:00,639
and I find that premise interesting.

30
00:03:01,223 --> 00:03:04,476
Surely you and Exception will be entering?

31
00:03:05,185 --> 00:03:06,061
I'm not sure.

32
00:03:09,315 --> 00:03:10,941
What do you think?

33
00:03:12,943 --> 00:03:13,861
Do you think…

34
00:03:16,405 --> 00:03:17,990
I should enter the competition?

35
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,169
Enter a cooking competition?

36
00:03:32,171 --> 00:03:33,213
Us?

37
00:03:34,089 --> 00:03:35,507
Yes, Auntie.

38
00:03:42,681 --> 00:03:43,599
Glad to work with you.

39
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:04,954
FAMIGLIA OWNER CHOI SONG-YI

40
00:04:05,037 --> 00:04:07,373
Chris K agreed to take part.

41
00:04:07,456 --> 00:04:09,541
Famiglia will enter the competition.

42
00:04:17,341 --> 00:04:19,385
The Table: K-Chef 2026

43
00:04:19,468 --> 00:04:22,096
isn't about selecting
Korea's best restaurant or dish.

44
00:04:22,179 --> 00:04:24,598
It's a competition to find
Korea's best chef.

45
00:04:24,682 --> 00:04:28,060
The focus isn't purely on
who cooks the best food.

46
00:04:28,143 --> 00:04:30,729
It's a survival competition
where teams will be evaluated

47
00:04:30,813 --> 00:04:33,107
on their creativity, interpretation
of the mission, and artistry.

48
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:36,902
Each team must be led by
a currently working Korean head chef,

49
00:04:36,986 --> 00:04:38,237
with four members in total.

50
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,531
You'll create a dish
that fits the challenge

51
00:04:40,614 --> 00:04:43,492
using only the allowed ingredients,
then present it to the judges.

52
00:04:43,575 --> 00:04:44,576
So far,

53
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:47,079
it sounds like most culinary competitions.

54
00:04:47,705 --> 00:04:50,165
That only covered the preliminary round.

55
00:04:50,249 --> 00:04:52,334
Listen to what comes next.

56
00:04:52,418 --> 00:04:55,462
First, a theme will be provided
in the form of a keyword.

57
00:04:55,546 --> 00:04:59,174
Participants will use this theme
to prepare for the main round.

58
00:05:01,010 --> 00:05:03,554
The main round takes place
a week later in the main studio,

59
00:05:03,637 --> 00:05:07,808
and that's when the details
about the theme and mission are provided.

60
00:05:07,891 --> 00:05:10,144
Then, each team will have three hours

61
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:12,730
to discuss, cook, and complete the dish.

62
00:05:13,272 --> 00:05:15,566
Once the dishes are served to the judges,

63
00:05:15,649 --> 00:05:18,694
each team's head chef
will give a presentation.

64
00:05:18,777 --> 00:05:22,072
The dish that best captures the theme

65
00:05:22,156 --> 00:05:25,617
or has the most creative interpretation
will receive the highest score.

66
00:05:26,493 --> 00:05:30,247
Of course,
the most important criterion is taste.

67
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:31,415
Sounds a bit tough, doesn't it?

68
00:05:32,416 --> 00:05:34,376
Not just a bit. It's insanely tough.

69
00:05:36,003 --> 00:05:38,172
-I wish they'd give an example.
-It can't be helped.

70
00:05:38,255 --> 00:05:41,008
This is what sets our competition apart,

71
00:05:41,091 --> 00:05:43,177
so we can't give you an example.

72
00:05:43,761 --> 00:05:46,221
The key is to anticipate and understand

73
00:05:46,305 --> 00:05:48,223
how the theme and mission
relate to each other.

74
00:05:48,724 --> 00:05:52,811
That's why the one-week preparation period
after the theme is announced is crucial.

75
00:05:52,895 --> 00:05:55,022
Oh, and about the head chef being Korean.

76
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:57,316
It's about heritage, not nationality.

77
00:05:57,399 --> 00:06:00,903
Anyone can enter as long as
one or both parents are Korean.

78
00:06:00,986 --> 00:06:02,571
I wish you luck then.

79
00:06:02,654 --> 00:06:04,364
I hope to see you at the main round!

80
00:06:04,448 --> 00:06:06,950
I, Captain Cook,
will keep honing my skills

81
00:06:07,034 --> 00:06:09,620
and do my best
to make it to the main round.

82
00:06:14,792 --> 00:06:16,376
I've watched it so many times

83
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:18,629
and I still have no idea
what they're talking about.

84
00:06:18,712 --> 00:06:20,672
They give us a theme as a keyword,

85
00:06:20,756 --> 00:06:24,760
and then a week later
we get a mission based on that theme.

86
00:06:24,843 --> 00:06:25,719
What does that mean?

87
00:06:26,678 --> 00:06:28,555
Couldn't they at least give an example?

88
00:06:29,223 --> 00:06:30,682
What kind of competition is this?

89
00:06:31,225 --> 00:06:33,060
Should I call some chefs I know?

90
00:06:33,143 --> 00:06:35,729
Someone out there
must've understood all that.

91
00:06:37,815 --> 00:06:40,984
I bet Pyeongyeon gave inside information
to chefs they're close with.

92
00:06:41,985 --> 00:06:42,861
Wait.

93
00:06:43,946 --> 00:06:46,490
Don't we have to pass the preliminaries

94
00:06:46,573 --> 00:06:49,201
before we can even worry about that?

95
00:06:49,993 --> 00:06:53,747
Let's focus on how we're going to
get through the preliminaries first.

96
00:06:54,248 --> 00:06:55,082
Okay.

97
00:06:55,165 --> 00:06:58,043
So the requirement is a team of four.

98
00:06:59,878 --> 00:07:01,922
But there are only two of us cooks.

99
00:07:05,551 --> 00:07:06,760
Yes…

100
00:07:07,594 --> 00:07:08,512
Just two.

101
00:07:15,602 --> 00:07:17,521
Can we even get someone?

102
00:07:18,647 --> 00:07:22,067
We've been trying to hire
kitchen staff for months.

103
00:07:23,944 --> 00:07:27,239
Unless they're dying to get on
Pyeongyeon Group's bad side…

104
00:07:29,741 --> 00:07:32,578
If we're really stuck,
we can hire part-timers as needed.

105
00:07:32,661 --> 00:07:33,787
Cooking is about teamwork.

106
00:07:34,913 --> 00:07:37,166
Only a well-trained team
that's practiced together

107
00:07:37,249 --> 00:07:38,834
can serve the best food.

108
00:07:40,377 --> 00:07:42,087
No matter how hard you work,

109
00:07:42,963 --> 00:07:45,674
no one person can handle
a competition of this size alone.

110
00:07:49,011 --> 00:07:50,596
Oh, dear…

111
00:08:01,273 --> 00:08:02,774
Can I help you?

112
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:05,235
Hello.

113
00:08:05,319 --> 00:08:09,406
I saw the notice outside
saying you're looking for kitchen staff.

114
00:08:16,663 --> 00:08:19,374
FAMIGLIA IS HIRING KITCHEN STAFF!

115
00:08:19,458 --> 00:08:25,255
PARK GEON-WOO
AGE 29

116
00:08:31,261 --> 00:08:34,223
Make yourself comfortable
and have some tea.

117
00:08:34,306 --> 00:08:35,515
Yes, thank you.

118
00:08:41,271 --> 00:08:43,607
"Studied culinary arts
at a community college

119
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:45,359
and started working at 21…"

120
00:08:45,442 --> 00:08:47,653
You started working in restaurants
at an early age.

121
00:08:47,736 --> 00:08:50,072
You even have
a traditional liquor sommelier license.

122
00:08:50,155 --> 00:08:54,284
You even opened your own restaurant at 23.

123
00:08:54,368 --> 00:08:55,619
How impressive.

124
00:08:55,702 --> 00:08:56,995
An Italian restaurant?

125
00:08:57,829 --> 00:09:03,001
Why did it close
after only about a year and a half?

126
00:09:03,085 --> 00:09:06,129
That was when COVID-19 spread.

127
00:09:06,672 --> 00:09:07,673
Oh, dear…

128
00:09:08,924 --> 00:09:10,884
What have you been doing
for the past four years?

129
00:09:13,303 --> 00:09:16,848
I spent a year paying off the debt
from closing the restaurant.

130
00:09:16,932 --> 00:09:19,226
After that…

131
00:09:20,310 --> 00:09:21,270
I took time off.

132
00:09:22,271 --> 00:09:24,147
So, no job?

133
00:09:24,231 --> 00:09:25,440
No.

134
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:28,902
Despite my short career as a cook,

135
00:09:30,112 --> 00:09:32,698
I felt burned out for some reason.

136
00:09:32,781 --> 00:09:35,659
I wasn't sure
if I wanted to stay on this path.

137
00:09:35,742 --> 00:09:39,871
I spent all the money
I had left traveling,

138
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:43,000
reading, and stuff like that.

139
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:47,170
Maybe what I needed
wasn't more technical training,

140
00:09:47,254 --> 00:09:51,800
but to learn more about people
and the world.

141
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:55,929
Enlightenment that comes
from studying, not training.

142
00:09:56,763 --> 00:09:58,598
That's what I hoped for.

143
00:10:00,142 --> 00:10:00,976
And?

144
00:10:02,686 --> 00:10:03,729
Were you enlightened?

145
00:10:04,229 --> 00:10:05,480
Yes.

146
00:10:07,774 --> 00:10:09,985
And what was that?

147
00:10:10,694 --> 00:10:11,611
It was

148
00:10:12,571 --> 00:10:13,613
that realization

149
00:10:14,364 --> 00:10:15,615
doesn't exist.

150
00:10:18,493 --> 00:10:20,162
I just wanted to return to the kitchen.

151
00:10:20,746 --> 00:10:22,039
Desperately too.

152
00:10:25,334 --> 00:10:26,877
Here are the details you asked for.

153
00:10:29,755 --> 00:10:32,841
It's our projected list of chefs
likely to make the main round.

154
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:40,891
Those missing a mark next to their names

155
00:10:40,974 --> 00:10:43,101
are yet to confirm their participation.

156
00:10:45,729 --> 00:10:47,939
A few chefs based overseas

157
00:10:48,023 --> 00:10:50,901
haven't yet confirmed by phone or email.

158
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:54,446
I'll have our overseas offices
meet them in person and secure them.

159
00:10:55,447 --> 00:10:56,490
Sounds good.

160
00:10:57,407 --> 00:10:58,909
It'll make for a pretty picture.

161
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:02,829
There's a good mix of domestic
and overseas participants.

162
00:11:02,913 --> 00:11:04,956
If you manage to cast Joshua Payton too,

163
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:06,666
it'll look great for our first show.

164
00:11:07,459 --> 00:11:08,460
Right.

165
00:11:08,543 --> 00:11:11,797
I'll persuade Joshua Yeong-ho Payton
no matter what it takes.

166
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:12,839
Good.

167
00:11:19,513 --> 00:11:20,597
Famiglia?

168
00:11:21,765 --> 00:11:23,392
Why are they on the list?

169
00:11:23,934 --> 00:11:25,894
They'll enter
when they don't even have a chef?

170
00:11:25,977 --> 00:11:27,562
And you think
they'll reach the main round?

171
00:11:28,313 --> 00:11:29,147
Yes.

172
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:38,782
Tell me why Famiglia is on the list.

173
00:11:39,366 --> 00:11:40,951
There are two reasons.

174
00:11:42,035 --> 00:11:47,666
First, they agreed to drop the lawsuit
against us in exchange for entering.

175
00:11:48,250 --> 00:11:49,459
They'll drop the suit?

176
00:11:49,543 --> 00:11:50,419
Yes.

177
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:55,549
Second, I'm using them
to get Cha Woo-jin to enter.

178
00:11:57,592 --> 00:12:02,222
Think of it as letting a shark loose
in a tank full of goldfish.

179
00:12:22,659 --> 00:12:23,493
Yeong-su.

180
00:12:23,994 --> 00:12:24,828
Yeah?

181
00:12:25,912 --> 00:12:27,706
Isn't that the sea bass
for tonight's main dish?

182
00:12:27,789 --> 00:12:28,623
It is.

183
00:12:29,541 --> 00:12:31,543
Why did you bring it out?
You don't cook the main dishes.

184
00:12:33,378 --> 00:12:35,797
The halibut for the ceviche
wasn't in good shape,

185
00:12:35,881 --> 00:12:38,216
so I thought we could serve
a sea bass salad instead.

186
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:40,886
I'm working on a sample
to take to Chef Cha.

187
00:12:43,555 --> 00:12:45,056
Oh, my bad.

188
00:12:45,849 --> 00:12:48,894
I was in a rush and forgot to tell you.

189
00:12:49,686 --> 00:12:51,062
Even if you were rushed…

190
00:12:52,147 --> 00:12:54,858
We prepared the exact amount needed.
You can't just take some.

191
00:12:54,941 --> 00:12:56,193
What are we to do now?

192
00:12:56,860 --> 00:12:58,528
I got it. I apologized.

193
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:06,495
Hey.

194
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:08,121
Hey, Michael.

195
00:13:09,414 --> 00:13:11,750
Jeez, that melodramatic jerk.

196
00:13:16,171 --> 00:13:17,797
I can't take this much longer.

197
00:13:26,765 --> 00:13:28,683
8 P.M. DINNER
ALLERGENS AND NOTES

198
00:13:34,231 --> 00:13:36,525
Chairman Park Myeong-gu
has a shellfish allergy.

199
00:13:36,608 --> 00:13:38,235
Why isn't that noted?

200
00:13:38,818 --> 00:13:40,487
Langoustine is the third course today.

201
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:42,030
LANGOUSTINE:
A SMALL LOBSTER

202
00:13:42,113 --> 00:13:43,406
I apologize, Chef.

203
00:13:43,490 --> 00:13:44,950
I left it out by mistake.

204
00:13:45,534 --> 00:13:47,160
Once is a mistake. Twice is a failure.

205
00:13:47,911 --> 00:13:49,204
Right. I'll be more careful.

206
00:13:56,419 --> 00:13:58,421
Don't you see the chairs are to one side?

207
00:13:59,381 --> 00:14:00,757
Measure the distance and rearrange them.

208
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:01,675
Yes, Chef.

209
00:14:03,093 --> 00:14:04,010
The flowers are wilted.

210
00:14:04,094 --> 00:14:06,054
Didn't you replace them this morning?

211
00:14:06,137 --> 00:14:07,055
Well…

212
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:09,140
If you have time to think, move!

213
00:14:09,224 --> 00:14:10,934
-Get fresh flowers.
-Yes, Chef.

214
00:14:24,447 --> 00:14:26,366
Lower the lighting two levels for dinner.

215
00:14:27,158 --> 00:14:28,326
I say this all the time.

216
00:14:28,410 --> 00:14:30,704
The dinner lighting should be
two settings lower than for lunch.

217
00:14:31,288 --> 00:14:32,205
No one can enjoy their wine

218
00:14:33,081 --> 00:14:34,541
under such bright lights.

219
00:14:35,542 --> 00:14:36,543
Keep in mind

220
00:14:36,626 --> 00:14:38,920
that fine dining
is as much about driving wine sales

221
00:14:39,004 --> 00:14:41,131
as it is about selling food.

222
00:14:41,715 --> 00:14:42,757
-Yes, Chef!
-Yes, Chef!

223
00:14:43,758 --> 00:14:44,926
Yes.

224
00:14:45,010 --> 00:14:46,678
As you can tell from the documents,

225
00:14:46,761 --> 00:14:49,514
all-you-can-eat dining
is popular these days.

226
00:14:50,015 --> 00:14:50,890
I see.

227
00:14:57,647 --> 00:14:58,815
Goodness.

228
00:14:59,858 --> 00:15:01,568
I didn't realize you had company.

229
00:15:04,237 --> 00:15:05,989
What could be so urgent

230
00:15:06,072 --> 00:15:08,742
that you came all the way
to the chairwoman's office, Ms. Seon?

231
00:15:09,951 --> 00:15:13,413
If you'd reported it to me,
I'd have brought it to her myself.

232
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:15,206
I asked to see her.

233
00:15:17,959 --> 00:15:21,713
I should get going now.
I have a meeting in ten minutes.

234
00:15:21,796 --> 00:15:22,631
Sure.

235
00:15:37,437 --> 00:15:39,856
You seem to be in a good mood.

236
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:42,651
Ms. Seon must be doing a good job.

237
00:15:44,235 --> 00:15:46,988
Even if you had urgent business with her,

238
00:15:47,072 --> 00:15:49,115
Seon Jeong-won works for me.

239
00:15:50,325 --> 00:15:53,787
Wouldn't it be nice
if she gave me a heads-up

240
00:15:54,412 --> 00:15:55,622
before coming to see you?

241
00:15:55,705 --> 00:15:56,581
What?

242
00:15:58,625 --> 00:15:59,459
Then again,

243
00:16:00,168 --> 00:16:02,545
Jeong-won is thorough
and good at what she does.

244
00:16:04,839 --> 00:16:08,343
Young people really know
how to get things done.

245
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:10,553
Old folks like me

246
00:16:10,637 --> 00:16:13,431
should sit at the back, watch, and clap.

247
00:16:18,478 --> 00:16:19,354
It's bitter.

248
00:16:19,896 --> 00:16:22,857
I'm left with an aftertaste
that's as bitter as my life.

249
00:16:24,442 --> 00:16:25,819
Mind if I have a candy?

250
00:16:31,574 --> 00:16:33,076
It's nice and sweet.

251
00:16:33,827 --> 00:16:36,246
Famiglia agreed to drop the lawsuit.

252
00:16:39,999 --> 00:16:41,960
They'll even enter the competition.

253
00:16:45,171 --> 00:16:46,423
Famiglia?

254
00:16:46,506 --> 00:16:48,425
How will they enter
when they don't even have a chef?

255
00:16:50,844 --> 00:16:52,804
That's the list of those
likely to reach the main round.

256
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:07,235
This is just nonsense.

257
00:17:08,695 --> 00:17:11,114
Seon Jeong-won, this brat…

258
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:13,700
Is she just really unrealistic,

259
00:17:13,783 --> 00:17:16,369
or is she trying to
create drama on purpose?

260
00:17:17,245 --> 00:17:18,872
This is absurd.

261
00:17:19,873 --> 00:17:23,042
It's fortunate that they dropped
the lawsuit before the competition…

262
00:17:27,172 --> 00:17:29,758
but we can't let Famiglia
gain any attention.

263
00:17:35,847 --> 00:17:37,766
Creating drama is fine,

264
00:17:37,849 --> 00:17:39,517
but the star of that show

265
00:17:40,310 --> 00:17:42,937
should be someone we cast,

266
00:17:43,021 --> 00:17:45,231
not some random outsider who wandered in.

267
00:17:49,402 --> 00:17:50,570
Don't you agree, Ms. Baek?

268
00:17:52,113 --> 00:17:53,448
Famiglia.

269
00:17:54,032 --> 00:17:56,659
Famiglia will enter the competition.

270
00:17:57,577 --> 00:17:59,287
Someone appeared at the last minute

271
00:17:59,370 --> 00:18:02,290
to take over a restaurant
that was on the verge of closing

272
00:18:02,373 --> 00:18:04,167
and is entering the competition.

273
00:18:05,251 --> 00:18:06,294
But who? Why?

274
00:18:06,377 --> 00:18:09,297
Not to mention,
they're projected to make the main round?

275
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:14,719
Famiglia is projected to
make the main round?

276
00:18:18,139 --> 00:18:21,017
Seeing as Seon Jeong-won
is frighteningly sharp…

277
00:18:26,147 --> 00:18:27,440
Send in Mr. Jeon.

278
00:18:28,316 --> 00:18:29,818
PARTICIPANTS LIKELY TO REACH MAIN ROUND

279
00:18:32,904 --> 00:18:34,155
Come in.

280
00:18:40,078 --> 00:18:41,120
You asked to see me, Ms. Baek?

281
00:18:42,330 --> 00:18:43,289
Take a seat.

282
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:49,212
I need you to look into something.

283
00:18:49,963 --> 00:18:51,005
Yes, ma'am.

284
00:18:52,048 --> 00:18:52,882
Famiglia.

285
00:18:52,966 --> 00:18:54,592
Famiglia?

286
00:18:56,511 --> 00:18:59,806
You mean the late Chef Choi's restaurant?

287
00:18:59,889 --> 00:19:00,849
Yes.

288
00:19:01,391 --> 00:19:03,059
That damn Famiglia.

289
00:19:04,561 --> 00:19:06,479
Someone random showed up in their kitchen

290
00:19:06,563 --> 00:19:09,607
like a gunslinger from the wilderness.

291
00:19:11,109 --> 00:19:13,903
Anyway, he seems to have some skill,

292
00:19:15,196 --> 00:19:19,033
seeing as he's entering the competition
as Famiglia's lead chef.

293
00:19:20,034 --> 00:19:21,995
Come on, Ms. Baek.

294
00:19:22,662 --> 00:19:24,664
That's impossible.

295
00:19:25,290 --> 00:19:28,501
The part head in charge of
prepping the ingredients quit,

296
00:19:28,585 --> 00:19:31,629
so there shouldn't be anyone left
except that useless lady.

297
00:19:36,217 --> 00:19:40,430
Find out quietly who this new chef is,

298
00:19:40,513 --> 00:19:43,433
where he came from, what he's been doing,

299
00:19:43,516 --> 00:19:45,560
how he's connected to Famiglia,

300
00:19:45,643 --> 00:19:48,396
and why he's entering the competition.

301
00:19:48,479 --> 00:19:49,731
Yes, ma'am.

302
00:19:49,814 --> 00:19:50,732
I'll do that.

303
00:19:50,815 --> 00:19:52,859
Don't hurry or get too rash.

304
00:19:52,942 --> 00:19:54,319
Do it properly.

305
00:19:55,653 --> 00:19:56,738
Mr. Jeon.

306
00:19:56,821 --> 00:19:58,114
Yes?

307
00:19:58,197 --> 00:20:01,993
If you mess up again
like you did with Choi Seung-hyo…

308
00:20:04,037 --> 00:20:05,413
you'll be done for.

309
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:07,540
I'll keep that in mind.

310
00:20:17,884 --> 00:20:19,260
Vegetable stew.

311
00:20:19,344 --> 00:20:20,386
It seems simple to make,

312
00:20:20,470 --> 00:20:23,306
but it's the ideal dish
to test one's basic skills.

313
00:20:52,335 --> 00:20:54,712
The ability to manage workspace
and hygiene.

314
00:21:27,078 --> 00:21:29,330
One person sautés the vegetables
over high heat

315
00:21:29,414 --> 00:21:30,873
and simmers the broth over low heat.

316
00:21:33,543 --> 00:21:35,044
The other does the opposite.

317
00:21:35,128 --> 00:21:37,046
She sautés the vegetables slowly
over low heat

318
00:21:37,130 --> 00:21:38,548
and cooks the broth over high heat.

319
00:21:41,217 --> 00:21:42,593
There is no right answer

320
00:21:42,677 --> 00:21:45,221
because cooking is ever-evolving.

321
00:21:48,182 --> 00:21:50,309
Auntie Du-yeong will be the sous-chef?

322
00:21:53,396 --> 00:21:57,066
To be fair,
Chef Park's stew tasted better.

323
00:21:57,734 --> 00:22:00,987
But the most important skills
for a sous-chef

324
00:22:01,070 --> 00:22:03,031
are workspace management
and hygiene.

325
00:22:04,198 --> 00:22:06,034
Everything must be clean
and well-organized,

326
00:22:06,117 --> 00:22:09,287
and the ingredients must be separated
so they are easily identified.

327
00:22:09,871 --> 00:22:12,331
Every second matters
in competitions like this,

328
00:22:12,415 --> 00:22:14,709
and those skills are absolutely essential
for the sous-chef.

329
00:22:16,794 --> 00:22:19,797
When it comes to prepping ingredients
and handling heat,

330
00:22:20,631 --> 00:22:22,675
Chef Park clearly had
more experience and practice.

331
00:22:23,426 --> 00:22:24,510
However,

332
00:22:24,594 --> 00:22:28,848
he lacks the skill to organize
and sort ingredients for easy use.

333
00:22:30,767 --> 00:22:32,351
It also depends on one's disposition.

334
00:22:33,227 --> 00:22:34,062
Chef Choi

335
00:22:34,937 --> 00:22:38,149
instinctively knows what to do and when.

336
00:22:42,153 --> 00:22:44,781
Therefore, Chef Choi Du-yeong
will be the sous-chef

337
00:22:45,448 --> 00:22:48,409
and Chef Park Geon-woo
will be the garde-manger.

338
00:22:49,577 --> 00:22:50,411
Yes, sir.

339
00:22:50,495 --> 00:22:53,956
We have a head chef,
sous-chef, and garde-manger.

340
00:22:55,374 --> 00:22:58,961
Now we need a commis
to handle odd jobs and dish-washing.

341
00:23:18,898 --> 00:23:19,816
I won't do it.

342
00:23:20,525 --> 00:23:21,609
I can't do it.

343
00:23:21,692 --> 00:23:23,319
Why can't you do it?

344
00:23:23,402 --> 00:23:24,320
Because…

345
00:23:25,863 --> 00:23:28,366
I just can't do it. I won't do it.

346
00:23:28,449 --> 00:23:30,827
I've never cooked before,
and I'm useless at it.

347
00:23:30,910 --> 00:23:31,744
On top of that,

348
00:23:32,328 --> 00:23:33,871
I don't even want to do this.

349
00:23:33,955 --> 00:23:35,206
I'm scared of knives.

350
00:23:35,289 --> 00:23:38,209
Do things that don't require using knives.
Wash the dishes.

351
00:23:38,292 --> 00:23:40,461
I still can't do it.

352
00:23:40,545 --> 00:23:41,921
I'm allergic.

353
00:23:42,630 --> 00:23:43,506
You're allergic?

354
00:23:44,132 --> 00:23:45,049
To what?

355
00:23:47,718 --> 00:23:48,719
To tap water.

356
00:23:49,387 --> 00:23:51,973
I'm allergic to tap water.
I can't even wash dishes.

357
00:23:52,598 --> 00:23:53,432
What?

358
00:23:54,016 --> 00:23:55,560
Anyway, I'm not doing it.

359
00:23:55,643 --> 00:23:57,061
I'm not entering the kitchen.

360
00:23:58,312 --> 00:23:59,147
Hey, Song.

361
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:03,359
You're allergic to tap water?

362
00:24:12,118 --> 00:24:13,828
I almost ended up in the kitchen.

363
00:24:15,705 --> 00:24:16,956
That would be a disaster.

364
00:24:17,832 --> 00:24:20,251
You season meat evenly on both sides.

365
00:24:20,835 --> 00:24:23,045
Beef steak should be flipped just once.

366
00:24:23,838 --> 00:24:27,008
Use black pepper by default
for its strong flavor and aroma,

367
00:24:27,091 --> 00:24:30,261
and use white pepper for lighter dishes
where black pepper could look messy.

368
00:24:30,344 --> 00:24:32,180
What are you talking about?

369
00:24:32,263 --> 00:24:33,723
Always sharpen knives with whetstones,

370
00:24:33,806 --> 00:24:36,225
once at 1,000 grit,
and then at 8,000.

371
00:24:36,309 --> 00:24:37,143
Excuse me?

372
00:24:37,226 --> 00:24:40,855
Boil dried pasta two or three minutes less
than the package says,

373
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:42,648
since it'll finish cooking in the pan.

374
00:24:43,691 --> 00:24:45,443
And always save the pasta water.

375
00:24:46,027 --> 00:24:48,863
Chef Krantzwerst.

376
00:24:48,946 --> 00:24:51,908
Memorize that much for now.
I'll teach you the rest in time.

377
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:54,785
The commis does the easy jobs anyway.

378
00:24:57,330 --> 00:24:59,957
And you can call me Chris.

379
00:25:00,750 --> 00:25:02,835
I won't cook, Chris.

380
00:25:02,919 --> 00:25:04,921
I own the restaurant and run the floor.

381
00:25:05,004 --> 00:25:06,297
I'm not a chef.

382
00:25:07,089 --> 00:25:08,049
Okay.

383
00:25:08,799 --> 00:25:09,634
So what?

384
00:25:10,384 --> 00:25:11,802
You can start learning.

385
00:25:12,845 --> 00:25:15,932
A restaurant owner
should know the basics of cooking.

386
00:25:16,015 --> 00:25:17,225
What if I refuse?

387
00:25:17,308 --> 00:25:18,434
Then find one.

388
00:25:18,517 --> 00:25:20,311
-Find what?
-Someone else.

389
00:25:22,563 --> 00:25:24,398
We need a team of four to enter.

390
00:25:24,482 --> 00:25:25,483
Are we not going to enter the competition?

391
00:25:26,776 --> 00:25:28,861
Even if we start practicing
around the clock now,

392
00:25:28,945 --> 00:25:30,321
there's no guarantee
we'll pass the preliminary round.

393
00:25:30,404 --> 00:25:33,074
You can't wait forever
for a kitchen hire that might never come.

394
00:25:37,620 --> 00:25:38,454
Hey.

395
00:25:39,413 --> 00:25:41,832
I don't want a cooking novice either.

396
00:25:42,959 --> 00:25:45,336
But right now, this is our only option.

397
00:25:51,008 --> 00:25:51,842
Hmm?

398
00:25:53,928 --> 00:25:54,804
Fine.

399
00:25:55,471 --> 00:25:58,766
But it's only until
we find my replacement.

400
00:25:58,849 --> 00:26:00,393
Once we hire new kitchen staff,

401
00:26:00,476 --> 00:26:02,311
I quit that instant.

402
00:26:06,274 --> 00:26:07,108
Okay.

403
00:26:07,858 --> 00:26:08,734
Deal.

404
00:26:23,457 --> 00:26:25,334
Who sprinkles salt from that height?

405
00:26:27,086 --> 00:26:28,838
Where did you learn to be that flashy?

406
00:26:28,921 --> 00:26:32,174
You sprinkle salt closely at eye level
so you get an even spread.

407
00:26:35,219 --> 00:26:37,847
I told you not to let the flame
extend past the pan!

408
00:26:38,681 --> 00:26:41,100
How many times did I tell you
it'll burn the sides?

409
00:26:42,977 --> 00:26:44,770
Adjust the flames to the size of the pan.

410
00:26:49,483 --> 00:26:50,860
Repeat after me.

411
00:26:50,943 --> 00:26:53,070
"Adjust the flames
to the size of the pan."

412
00:26:53,946 --> 00:26:55,740
"Adjust the flames to the size of…"

413
00:26:55,823 --> 00:26:57,074
Louder!

414
00:26:57,658 --> 00:27:00,411
"Adjust the flames
to the size of the pan!"

415
00:27:02,663 --> 00:27:05,291
I told you,
the meat goes in at the smoking point.

416
00:27:05,374 --> 00:27:08,294
Coat the pan with oil
and once it starts to smoke like crazy,

417
00:27:08,377 --> 00:27:09,587
count to 20, then add the meat.

418
00:27:11,172 --> 00:27:12,006
That's not the right sizzle.

419
00:27:13,591 --> 00:27:14,842
We want a loud sizzling sound.

420
00:27:14,925 --> 00:27:16,802
No sound, no color.

421
00:27:16,886 --> 00:27:18,721
No color, no taste. Okay?

422
00:27:30,649 --> 00:27:31,901
By the way,

423
00:27:33,110 --> 00:27:34,820
can you not use English?

424
00:27:34,904 --> 00:27:37,323
My head's already a mess
with all I have to learn.

425
00:27:38,949 --> 00:27:40,034
Huh?

426
00:27:40,117 --> 00:27:44,580
Your English is so fluent and native
that I can barely understand it.

427
00:27:44,663 --> 00:27:46,415
You don't need to be flashy.

428
00:27:46,499 --> 00:27:48,542
Let's do it the Korean way.

429
00:27:54,298 --> 00:27:56,384
Back straight, chin up.

430
00:28:03,724 --> 00:28:04,975
This is madness.

431
00:28:05,059 --> 00:28:06,852
What if someone gets hurt?

432
00:28:07,645 --> 00:28:10,106
I told you to be extra cautious
when you're holding a knife.

433
00:28:11,899 --> 00:28:12,858
What did I say earlier?

434
00:28:13,442 --> 00:28:14,527
The three-finger rule.

435
00:28:15,194 --> 00:28:17,446
Your hand should be like this,
curled at the first joint.

436
00:28:19,532 --> 00:28:21,200
Curl it even further.

437
00:28:22,368 --> 00:28:23,285
Hold it like this.

438
00:28:24,203 --> 00:28:25,121
Watch carefully.

439
00:28:26,080 --> 00:28:28,040
Grip the knife farther forward.

440
00:28:29,708 --> 00:28:30,751
Closer to the blade.

441
00:28:34,380 --> 00:28:38,092
When slicing,
push the blade gently forward.

442
00:28:40,678 --> 00:28:43,013
Use the weight of the knife, like this.

443
00:29:03,659 --> 00:29:04,702
Do you see that?

444
00:29:24,180 --> 00:29:26,474
Why are you so startled?
It's just a light cut.

445
00:29:27,725 --> 00:29:28,559
See?

446
00:29:28,642 --> 00:29:29,935
See what?

447
00:29:30,019 --> 00:29:32,480
I told you I shouldn't be in the kitchen.

448
00:29:32,563 --> 00:29:34,190
This is why I didn't want to cook.

449
00:29:53,167 --> 00:29:54,084
Oh dear.

450
00:29:55,044 --> 00:29:57,630
Try to understand.
She has her reasons.

451
00:29:57,713 --> 00:29:58,839
What?

452
00:29:58,923 --> 00:30:01,926
Ms. Choi never sets foot in the kitchen.

453
00:30:03,135 --> 00:30:05,513
Why not? Does she never cook then?

454
00:30:06,388 --> 00:30:09,683
She eats what someone else cooked,
eats out, or orders in.

455
00:30:11,936 --> 00:30:12,937
Well, you see…

456
00:30:16,774 --> 00:30:17,858
It's the ghost.

457
00:30:18,984 --> 00:30:19,860
A ghost?

458
00:30:19,944 --> 00:30:21,445
The thing is,

459
00:30:23,531 --> 00:30:24,532
there's a ghost…

460
00:30:26,575 --> 00:30:27,910
on her shoulders.

461
00:30:30,746 --> 00:30:32,164
It's an inside joke of sorts.

462
00:30:32,248 --> 00:30:35,167
You're too American to get it
even if I were to explain.

463
00:30:51,058 --> 00:30:53,018
This was my dad's room.

464
00:30:53,102 --> 00:30:55,854
I got rid of his clothes
and most of his stuff

465
00:30:56,730 --> 00:30:57,940
but the furniture stayed.

466
00:31:22,506 --> 00:31:23,382
What's wrong?

467
00:31:24,091 --> 00:31:24,967
Huh?

468
00:31:27,761 --> 00:31:28,762
It's nothing.

469
00:31:30,055 --> 00:31:32,266
The bathroom's to the right.

470
00:31:32,349 --> 00:31:33,934
My room is across the hall,

471
00:31:34,018 --> 00:31:35,561
so knock if you need anything.

472
00:31:43,027 --> 00:31:44,194
If you want coffee,

473
00:31:44,278 --> 00:31:46,572
there's a machine next to the sink.

474
00:31:46,655 --> 00:31:49,491
The instructions are on the wall,
so you shouldn't have any issues using it.

475
00:31:50,451 --> 00:31:51,327
Okay.

476
00:31:57,416 --> 00:31:58,584
What's that?

477
00:32:01,045 --> 00:32:02,338
It's my friend.

478
00:32:12,222 --> 00:32:15,559
Are you sure
you don't have to go back to the US?

479
00:32:16,268 --> 00:32:18,729
You said something
about a breach of contract.

480
00:32:20,272 --> 00:32:22,983
I told them I'd pay a penalty
in return for staying three more months.

481
00:32:23,776 --> 00:32:25,069
The prize money is 500 million won.

482
00:32:25,736 --> 00:32:27,237
I'll pay the penalty with some of that.

483
00:32:28,238 --> 00:32:29,114
What?

484
00:32:29,198 --> 00:32:30,616
Song-yi!

485
00:32:30,699 --> 00:32:32,951
Song-yi! The front door's jammed again.

486
00:32:33,035 --> 00:32:34,411
-Get over here!
-Okay, Auntie.

487
00:32:35,371 --> 00:32:36,705
I left my phone downstairs.

488
00:32:37,623 --> 00:32:39,166
I'm coming, Auntie!

489
00:32:45,714 --> 00:32:46,840
Am I doing the right thing?

490
00:32:53,222 --> 00:32:54,473
I should do this, right?

491
00:32:56,809 --> 00:32:59,144
Have a wonderful day.

492
00:33:26,755 --> 00:33:29,591
Should we call this Korean cuisine?

493
00:33:30,134 --> 00:33:31,218
Or is it Japanese cuisine?

494
00:33:31,301 --> 00:33:32,136
Or is it

495
00:33:33,095 --> 00:33:34,012
French?

496
00:33:37,766 --> 00:33:39,977
It's none of those.

497
00:33:40,644 --> 00:33:43,731
It's simply a dish made by a Korean chef.

498
00:33:44,606 --> 00:33:49,319
I think national boundaries around cuisine
are a thing of the past.

499
00:33:49,987 --> 00:33:52,406
We need to look at it more closely now.

500
00:33:53,699 --> 00:33:57,494
Our aim is to find a universality
within what is Korean.

501
00:33:57,578 --> 00:34:00,164
Through that process, we can discover

502
00:34:00,247 --> 00:34:03,542
the identity of Korean cuisine
and its future.

503
00:34:04,501 --> 00:34:07,129
The point is,
we're looking for the best Korean chef

504
00:34:07,212 --> 00:34:09,256
and not the best Korean dish.

505
00:34:09,840 --> 00:34:12,009
In the end,
it's the people we're interested in.

506
00:34:12,968 --> 00:34:17,264
We won't be able to define
what K-food is with this one competition.

507
00:34:17,347 --> 00:34:19,808
But if we keep the focus on the people,

508
00:34:19,892 --> 00:34:23,562
we'll gradually develop
a clearer standard for what K-food is

509
00:34:24,313 --> 00:34:25,606
and what it should be like.

510
00:34:33,989 --> 00:34:34,865
Is there anything else you need?

511
00:34:35,699 --> 00:34:36,575
How was the food?

512
00:34:37,242 --> 00:34:38,410
It suited the name of the restaurant.

513
00:34:39,620 --> 00:34:40,579
It was exceptional.

514
00:34:58,847 --> 00:35:00,808
I assume Famiglia
will be closing down soon.

515
00:35:07,648 --> 00:35:08,816
They might not close down.

516
00:35:12,945 --> 00:35:14,112
They won't close down?

517
00:35:15,155 --> 00:35:19,535
They found a new head chef
to take over the kitchen.

518
00:35:22,579 --> 00:35:24,164
Who is this new chef?

519
00:35:24,957 --> 00:35:27,709
He's a rising star
in the US and Europe right now.

520
00:35:28,585 --> 00:35:30,671
He's a Korean chef named Chris K.

521
00:35:31,713 --> 00:35:34,508
He's based in New York,
but he's in Korea right now.

522
00:35:34,591 --> 00:35:36,176
That very Chris K…

523
00:35:39,263 --> 00:35:40,472
had agreed to lead Famiglia

524
00:35:41,682 --> 00:35:44,726
in The Table: K-Chef 2026.

525
00:37:10,896 --> 00:37:12,147
Keep the peel thin.

526
00:37:12,230 --> 00:37:13,106
Okay.

527
00:37:20,030 --> 00:37:21,531
No. Turn off the stove.

528
00:37:24,117 --> 00:37:25,285
What did I say earlier?

529
00:37:25,369 --> 00:37:26,536
When you baste with butter,

530
00:37:26,620 --> 00:37:29,081
do it quickly and continuously
for 30 to 35 times.

531
00:37:29,164 --> 00:37:30,707
Then you flip it and baste
another 20 to 25 times.

532
00:37:32,042 --> 00:37:33,001
Chef Park, come and watch.

533
00:37:33,877 --> 00:37:34,711
Okay.

534
00:37:37,172 --> 00:37:39,341
The reason we arroser with refined butter

535
00:37:39,424 --> 00:37:41,343
is to speed up the Maillard reaction.

536
00:37:41,426 --> 00:37:43,220
So you must do it at a regular speed.

537
00:37:43,845 --> 00:37:46,556
As fast as possible, at an even rhythm.

538
00:37:47,224 --> 00:37:49,351
That's why we don't put
more than two pieces of meat in a pan.

539
00:37:49,434 --> 00:37:51,269
It's hard to arroser three at once.

540
00:37:53,313 --> 00:37:56,400
You'll continue to practice
until you can tell the right temperature

541
00:37:56,483 --> 00:37:57,818
without a thermometer.

542
00:37:59,027 --> 00:38:00,237
Got it?

543
00:38:00,821 --> 00:38:02,572
If you can't do that,
we won't pass the preliminaries,

544
00:38:02,656 --> 00:38:04,783
let alone win the competition. Okay?

545
00:38:05,492 --> 00:38:06,368
-Okay.
-Okay.

546
00:38:07,411 --> 00:38:09,287
What? Win the competition?

547
00:38:10,872 --> 00:38:12,207
Yeah. Win the whole thing.

548
00:38:18,463 --> 00:38:20,590
Why, what's the matter?
You don't want to win?

549
00:38:21,174 --> 00:38:23,677
Why enter if not to win?
Do you have that much time to waste?

550
00:38:23,760 --> 00:38:24,845
-Well…
-No, but…

551
00:38:26,680 --> 00:38:28,056
Get back to work.

552
00:38:28,140 --> 00:38:30,100
The longer food takes to serve,
the worse it tastes.

553
00:38:30,183 --> 00:38:33,770
The customers don't taste food
with just their tongues and mouths.

554
00:38:34,354 --> 00:38:35,564
They feel it with their hearts.

555
00:38:36,565 --> 00:38:39,317
If the food is late,
you've already lost them.

556
00:38:40,235 --> 00:38:42,487
All right, get back to it. Let's go.

557
00:38:42,571 --> 00:38:43,822
-Yes, Chef!
-Yes, Chef!

558
00:38:58,503 --> 00:38:59,337
Mr. Park?

559
00:39:00,922 --> 00:39:03,675
You can't leave
the sauces and broth out like this.

560
00:39:03,759 --> 00:39:05,260
Put them back where they belong.

561
00:39:05,343 --> 00:39:06,887
Oh, okay.

562
00:39:06,970 --> 00:39:08,722
I was going to do that
after I rinsed this.

563
00:39:08,805 --> 00:39:10,766
There's an order to everything.

564
00:39:10,849 --> 00:39:13,935
You store the ingredients away
before you wash any dishes.

565
00:39:16,730 --> 00:39:18,065
Okay.

566
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:21,735
Why didn't you dry your hands?

567
00:39:22,360 --> 00:39:24,404
Don't you see water dripping on the floor?

568
00:39:24,488 --> 00:39:27,032
What if someone slips and gets hurt?

569
00:39:28,617 --> 00:39:30,160
A few drops won't make anyone slip.

570
00:39:30,243 --> 00:39:31,703
"A few drops"?

571
00:39:31,787 --> 00:39:33,830
Didn't you hear what Chef Chris said?

572
00:39:33,914 --> 00:39:34,956
We have rules.

573
00:39:36,541 --> 00:39:37,584
Yes, Chef.

574
00:39:40,253 --> 00:39:41,129
What's that?

575
00:39:42,297 --> 00:39:45,217
You can't leave the pans like that
after they're washed.

576
00:39:45,300 --> 00:39:47,803
-Wipe them with a dry cloth…
-I was going to do,

577
00:39:47,886 --> 00:39:50,305
but you told me
to put away the sauce bottles.

578
00:39:50,388 --> 00:39:52,724
Don't you know cast iron pans rust
if they're not dried right away?

579
00:39:52,808 --> 00:39:55,268
You should know that.
It's basic knowledge.

580
00:39:55,352 --> 00:39:56,478
Listen, lady.

581
00:40:00,107 --> 00:40:02,609
How long have you been cooking for?

582
00:40:03,777 --> 00:40:04,611
A year? Two?

583
00:40:05,821 --> 00:40:08,323
I worked in a kitchen
for over eight years.

584
00:40:09,491 --> 00:40:12,869
I know my way around one
and how things work.

585
00:40:12,953 --> 00:40:15,205
I can't understand why the head chef

586
00:40:15,288 --> 00:40:17,916
named you the sous-chef,

587
00:40:17,999 --> 00:40:20,001
but I respect his decision.

588
00:40:21,169 --> 00:40:24,256
However, I have my own rules
and my own way of doing things.

589
00:40:24,339 --> 00:40:27,300
I'd appreciate it if you respected that.

590
00:40:28,426 --> 00:40:30,345
Also, let me say just one thing.

591
00:40:30,929 --> 00:40:33,765
When you rest meat,
flip it once halfway through.

592
00:40:33,849 --> 00:40:35,433
Don't leave it sitting on one side.

593
00:40:35,517 --> 00:40:38,770
That's how you get the juice
to permeate the whole steak.

594
00:40:39,354 --> 00:40:42,232
You should know that much
if you're the sous-chef.

595
00:41:31,072 --> 00:41:31,907
Who are you?

596
00:41:34,826 --> 00:41:35,744
What brings you here?

597
00:41:50,258 --> 00:41:51,092
So it's you.

598
00:41:59,559 --> 00:42:00,560
Chris K.

599
00:42:08,860 --> 00:42:11,196
You're almost revered in the US.

600
00:42:11,905 --> 00:42:14,199
Why are you
hanging around a dump like this?

601
00:42:15,575 --> 00:42:16,534
Care to explain?

602
00:42:16,618 --> 00:42:18,995
Why should I explain myself to you?

603
00:42:23,124 --> 00:42:24,793
You were rude to me first.

604
00:42:27,504 --> 00:42:28,421
If you have nothing to say…

605
00:42:33,510 --> 00:42:34,386
Why did you come here?

606
00:42:36,221 --> 00:42:37,639
What's your connection to Famiglia?

607
00:42:39,683 --> 00:42:40,892
I hear you're entering the competition.

608
00:42:49,442 --> 00:42:50,277
Then again…

609
00:42:52,362 --> 00:42:53,780
I guess none of that really matters.

610
00:42:57,158 --> 00:42:58,118
What matters is…

611
00:43:00,578 --> 00:43:03,498
who wins in the end.

612
00:43:06,251 --> 00:43:08,670
Seeing as Pyeongyeon rushed
to put the competition together,

613
00:43:08,753 --> 00:43:10,755
I was expecting a few stragglers.

614
00:43:12,215 --> 00:43:13,466
I'm glad I was wrong.

615
00:43:14,592 --> 00:43:15,719
This should be interesting.

616
00:43:16,636 --> 00:43:18,596
I'll see you soon, buddy.

617
00:43:21,224 --> 00:43:22,058
Hey.

618
00:43:24,394 --> 00:43:25,603
Don't worry.

619
00:43:29,941 --> 00:43:30,984
Because in the end,

620
00:43:31,943 --> 00:43:33,153
you'll lose to me again anyway.

621
00:43:34,446 --> 00:43:35,655
Just like you did seven years ago.

622
00:43:39,284 --> 00:43:40,243
And

623
00:43:42,120 --> 00:43:43,455
you'll regret it.

624
00:43:47,167 --> 00:43:48,835
You'll regret what you did that day.

625
00:44:08,938 --> 00:44:10,273
No.

626
00:44:25,038 --> 00:44:27,040
Song-yi. Are you going somewhere?

627
00:44:28,541 --> 00:44:30,668
I'm just going out for a short while.

628
00:44:31,586 --> 00:44:32,754
Where are you going?

629
00:44:34,089 --> 00:44:35,423
We need to start practicing.

630
00:44:36,383 --> 00:44:38,259
Sorry. It's really urgent.

631
00:44:38,885 --> 00:44:39,969
Let's start practicing tomorrow.

632
00:44:44,599 --> 00:44:45,934
We don't have that much time.

633
00:44:47,268 --> 00:44:48,311
Can we start tomorrow?

634
00:44:48,895 --> 00:44:51,022
I'll work really hard, I promise.

635
00:44:52,649 --> 00:44:55,985
Please. Just for one day. Today.

636
00:45:01,032 --> 00:45:01,866
Okay.

637
00:45:01,950 --> 00:45:02,784
Okay.

638
00:45:12,085 --> 00:45:13,503
I am worried though.

639
00:45:15,088 --> 00:45:17,132
That Song-yi has to work in the kitchen.

640
00:45:21,219 --> 00:45:24,556
It was somewhat
of an open secret at Famiglia

641
00:45:25,348 --> 00:45:27,267
that she's haunted by a ghost.

642
00:45:27,350 --> 00:45:28,184
A ghost?

643
00:45:28,893 --> 00:45:30,353
Like a ghost?

644
00:45:31,020 --> 00:45:32,230
Ms. Choi

645
00:45:33,148 --> 00:45:34,566
is haunted by a ghost?

646
00:45:34,649 --> 00:45:35,775
Yes.

647
00:45:35,859 --> 00:45:37,694
At first, no one thought much of it,

648
00:45:37,777 --> 00:45:40,905
thinking it was just some coincidence.

649
00:46:06,973 --> 00:46:08,141
Here you go, Chef.

650
00:46:09,184 --> 00:46:11,144
This is just what I was looking for.

651
00:46:11,769 --> 00:46:13,855
Look at our sweet little Song-yi.

652
00:46:13,938 --> 00:46:16,191
You're always one step ahead, aren't you?

653
00:46:24,240 --> 00:46:27,327
-Chef, can I help you?
-Will you?

654
00:46:27,911 --> 00:46:31,247
Then can you keep stirring this slowly
so the sauce doesn't set?

655
00:46:31,331 --> 00:46:33,291
-Yes, Chef.
-Thanks a lot.

656
00:46:34,250 --> 00:46:36,002
-It's hot, so be careful.
-Okay.

657
00:46:36,085 --> 00:46:38,129
You're going to make a great chef someday.

658
00:46:38,755 --> 00:46:40,006
Your dad must be proud.

659
00:46:40,089 --> 00:46:42,091
You're way better than her dad, actually.

660
00:46:42,175 --> 00:46:43,593
You're doing better than he is.

661
00:46:53,728 --> 00:46:55,355
Jun-ho!

662
00:46:56,856 --> 00:46:58,650
Get some ice and a dry towel, quick.

663
00:46:59,484 --> 00:47:01,027
The skin's peeling already.

664
00:47:01,110 --> 00:47:02,779
Forget it. Take him to the ER.

665
00:47:02,862 --> 00:47:05,240
-Put some ice on the wound.
-Okay.

666
00:47:05,323 --> 00:47:06,783
Careful. Watch out.

667
00:47:14,958 --> 00:47:16,292
Strangely enough,

668
00:47:16,376 --> 00:47:18,628
every time Song-yi went into the kitchen,

669
00:47:19,504 --> 00:47:21,881
someone would get hurt.

670
00:47:21,965 --> 00:47:23,841
And quite badly too.

671
00:47:32,767 --> 00:47:34,519
Knife cuts were the least of it.

672
00:47:45,989 --> 00:47:47,240
Contusions.

673
00:47:58,876 --> 00:47:59,877
Hey!

674
00:48:03,756 --> 00:48:04,716
Burns.

675
00:48:09,429 --> 00:48:12,098
A customer at table three
is allergic to short-necked clams.

676
00:48:12,181 --> 00:48:13,224
What should we do?

677
00:48:13,808 --> 00:48:15,602
Tell them we'll take out the clams,

678
00:48:15,685 --> 00:48:17,854
but that we'll add
more mushrooms and vegetables.

679
00:48:17,937 --> 00:48:19,856
-And serve it with extra cream.
-Yes, Chef.

680
00:48:26,112 --> 00:48:27,363
Broken bones.

681
00:48:46,716 --> 00:48:49,594
Even breathing difficulties

682
00:48:51,346 --> 00:48:52,722
and full-body paralysis.

683
00:48:59,646 --> 00:49:04,275
Too many people got hurt
to call it a mere coincidence.

684
00:49:05,443 --> 00:49:06,986
The reason for all that was…

685
00:49:07,070 --> 00:49:08,946
There's a ghost sitting on you.

686
00:49:09,906 --> 00:49:12,408
It's sitting right on your shoulders.

687
00:49:17,664 --> 00:49:19,540
It's obsessed with fire.

688
00:49:20,166 --> 00:49:24,170
It's even carrying a huge knife,
and you had no idea?

689
00:49:24,253 --> 00:49:25,838
Stay away from fire,

690
00:49:26,714 --> 00:49:29,342
especially those in kitchens or on stoves.

691
00:49:29,425 --> 00:49:32,970
The sight of fire
sends the ghost into a frenzy.

692
00:49:33,054 --> 00:49:35,431
When it starts swinging its knife around,

693
00:49:36,057 --> 00:49:39,268
it won't be you who gets hurt,
but those around you.

694
00:49:39,352 --> 00:49:40,520
Remember that.

695
00:49:41,896 --> 00:49:43,398
Never go near a kitchen.

696
00:49:43,940 --> 00:49:45,191
Ever.

697
00:49:47,527 --> 00:49:50,071
She didn't understand what it meant,
but it left her uneasy.

698
00:49:50,154 --> 00:49:51,989
So instead of
going into the kitchen that day,

699
00:49:52,073 --> 00:49:54,325
she stayed upstairs watching TV.

700
00:49:54,409 --> 00:49:57,286
But it so happened
that the restaurant was packed that day,

701
00:49:57,870 --> 00:50:00,331
and the kitchen needed some extra help.

702
00:50:02,458 --> 00:50:03,668
Bring me some more stock.

703
00:50:03,751 --> 00:50:04,961
-Yes, Chef!
-Yes, Chef!

704
00:50:17,056 --> 00:50:18,057
I need stock!

705
00:50:18,141 --> 00:50:20,768
Three of the eight salads
will be ready in three minutes.

706
00:50:21,269 --> 00:50:22,895
The dill is prepped and ready.

707
00:50:22,979 --> 00:50:24,313
Where's the fresh chervil?

708
00:50:24,397 --> 00:50:27,108
Can someone confirm what mains
tables five and six ordered?

709
00:51:13,988 --> 00:51:16,365
He was rushed to the ER and treated,

710
00:51:17,825 --> 00:51:20,286
then transferred to a special burn unit.

711
00:51:22,038 --> 00:51:23,664
He had third-degree burns on his left leg.

712
00:51:24,248 --> 00:51:26,542
Part of his muscles and nerves
were badly damaged,

713
00:51:26,626 --> 00:51:30,254
so he did rehab for six months
after his surgery.

714
00:51:30,880 --> 00:51:32,381
He even got skin grafts.

715
00:51:34,175 --> 00:51:35,301
That's when

716
00:51:35,384 --> 00:51:38,346
my late brother
started walking with a limp.

717
00:51:41,057 --> 00:51:42,600
That guilt

718
00:51:43,309 --> 00:51:46,604
is probably why Song-yi took
such devoted care of her father.

719
00:51:48,356 --> 00:51:49,690
Do you get it now?

720
00:51:50,650 --> 00:51:52,944
Why she refuses to go into the kitchen?

721
00:52:04,664 --> 00:52:06,374
Do you know someone
who can do the job for you?

722
00:52:06,457 --> 00:52:07,416
The job?

723
00:52:08,709 --> 00:52:09,544
What job?

724
00:52:09,627 --> 00:52:10,878
A shamanic ritual.

725
00:52:11,546 --> 00:52:13,756
Oh, you mean a gut?

726
00:52:14,507 --> 00:52:16,884
No man can chase away a ghost.

727
00:52:16,968 --> 00:52:18,719
You need the deities' help.

728
00:52:20,972 --> 00:52:21,889
I see.

729
00:52:33,442 --> 00:52:36,988
It looks like
I'll have to call on several deities.

730
00:52:37,071 --> 00:52:38,239
It'll cost you.

731
00:52:39,991 --> 00:52:41,242
How much?

732
00:52:41,868 --> 00:52:42,994
Let's see.

733
00:52:46,080 --> 00:52:49,333
Dear deities, I ask for your guidance.

734
00:52:50,626 --> 00:52:52,795
Rat, ox, tiger, rabbit, dragon, snake,
horse, goat, monkey, rooster, dog, pig.

735
00:52:52,879 --> 00:52:56,090
Gab, eul, byeong, jeong,
mu, gi, gyeong, shin, im, gye.

736
00:52:57,800 --> 00:53:01,429
Give me an auspicious date where we can

737
00:53:01,512 --> 00:53:04,724
eliminate the bad energy
and leave the good!

738
00:53:08,603 --> 00:53:09,437
Fifteen million.

739
00:53:09,520 --> 00:53:10,479
What?

740
00:53:11,522 --> 00:53:12,607
Fifteen million won?

741
00:53:16,611 --> 00:53:18,821
I don't have 1.5 million won,
let alone 15 million.

742
00:53:22,366 --> 00:53:23,576
Mister.

743
00:53:24,911 --> 00:53:26,454
I'm sorry,

744
00:53:27,538 --> 00:53:29,540
but is there any way
you could give me a discount?

745
00:53:38,591 --> 00:53:40,468
Rat, ox, tiger, rabbit, dragon, snake,
horse, goat, monkey, rooster, dog, pig.

746
00:53:40,551 --> 00:53:44,221
Gab, eul, byeong, jeong,
mu, gi, gyeong, shin, im, gye.

747
00:53:46,807 --> 00:53:49,518
Wood feeds fire, water overcomes fire,

748
00:53:49,602 --> 00:53:51,479
earth generates metal,
metal generates water…

749
00:53:53,105 --> 00:53:53,940
Ten million!

750
00:53:56,233 --> 00:53:57,109
Ten million won?

751
00:54:05,993 --> 00:54:09,038
Rat, ox, tiger, rabbit,
dragon, snake, horse, goat…

752
00:54:09,121 --> 00:54:10,957
Five million won. That's it.

753
00:54:12,208 --> 00:54:13,125
Mister.

754
00:54:13,960 --> 00:54:15,378
I'm really sorry,

755
00:54:16,671 --> 00:54:19,799
but I don't think I can afford a ritual.

756
00:54:20,883 --> 00:54:23,970
Is there anything you can do
as a temporary fix?

757
00:54:25,221 --> 00:54:28,557
I just need to work in the kitchen
until the competition's over.

758
00:54:30,893 --> 00:54:33,771
Please, Mister. I need your help.

759
00:54:37,984 --> 00:54:39,235
It's a temporary talisman.

760
00:54:40,027 --> 00:54:42,405
Keep it in your pocket wherever you go.

761
00:54:42,989 --> 00:54:45,491
It'll subdue
the ghost's energy for a while.

762
00:54:46,075 --> 00:54:47,368
But you must remember.

763
00:54:48,119 --> 00:54:49,745
The effects of a temporary talisman

764
00:54:50,538 --> 00:54:52,957
don't last very long.

765
00:54:54,417 --> 00:54:55,334
Okay.

766
00:54:55,918 --> 00:54:56,919
Thank you.

767
00:54:58,254 --> 00:54:59,505
So…

768
00:55:00,172 --> 00:55:03,467
How much is the talisman?

769
00:55:04,093 --> 00:55:06,929
You don't exactly look like
you have money to spare.

770
00:55:07,596 --> 00:55:09,515
Just pay a decent fee.

771
00:55:10,391 --> 00:55:11,434
Would that be okay?

772
00:55:16,689 --> 00:55:19,150
-Thank you. Thanks very much.
-Wait…

773
00:55:21,402 --> 00:55:23,529
Goodness…

774
00:55:24,864 --> 00:55:27,116
It's hard to make a living these days.

775
00:55:27,199 --> 00:55:30,036
FREE MEAL COUPON

776
00:55:30,745 --> 00:55:31,954
Free food, huh?

777
00:56:14,371 --> 00:56:18,084
I watch you climb sometimes and wonder,

778
00:56:19,794 --> 00:56:21,003
"Why go through all that trouble

779
00:56:22,338 --> 00:56:25,883
when she has to come back down anyway?"

780
00:56:30,137 --> 00:56:31,847
But having a goal you can actually see…

781
00:56:34,475 --> 00:56:35,726
is something to be happy about.

782
00:56:40,481 --> 00:56:41,440
We'll enter as well.

783
00:56:43,609 --> 00:56:45,194
The Table: K-Chef 2026.

784
00:56:45,277 --> 00:56:47,488
Exception and I, Cha Woo-jin.

785
00:56:50,783 --> 00:56:53,285
What? You're not happy?

786
00:56:54,662 --> 00:56:55,913
I thought you'd be thrilled.

787
00:56:56,580 --> 00:56:57,998
I guess I got carried away.

788
00:57:05,798 --> 00:57:06,715
I am happy.

789
00:57:08,634 --> 00:57:09,844
I'm really happy.

790
00:57:12,513 --> 00:57:13,973
Thank you, Woo-jin…

791
00:57:15,683 --> 00:57:17,017
for joining the show.

792
00:57:22,481 --> 00:57:23,524
Yes, of course.

793
00:57:23,607 --> 00:57:26,569
There will be a pantry
filled with the necessary ingredients.

794
00:57:26,652 --> 00:57:28,904
You can only use what's provided there.

795
00:57:28,988 --> 00:57:32,199
-Yes. That's just…
-It has to be Wednesday.

796
00:57:32,283 --> 00:57:34,368
I need you to be free this Wednesday.

797
00:57:34,451 --> 00:57:35,786
That goes for your teammates too.

798
00:57:35,870 --> 00:57:37,329
The time…

799
00:57:37,413 --> 00:57:39,415
Once we know the main-round contestants,

800
00:57:39,498 --> 00:57:42,334
we'll let you know the exact schedule.

801
00:59:25,980 --> 00:59:27,815
CHOI SONG-YI

802
00:59:40,953 --> 00:59:42,329
Thank you again

803
00:59:42,413 --> 00:59:44,373
for making such a tough decision,
Ms. Choi.

804
00:59:46,667 --> 00:59:47,501
And…

805
00:59:48,669 --> 00:59:50,421
I wish you the best of luck.

806
00:59:51,672 --> 00:59:52,673
I mean it.

807
00:59:54,800 --> 00:59:55,676
LIST OF PARTICIPANTS

808
00:59:55,759 --> 00:59:57,052
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

809
01:00:35,758 --> 01:00:37,468
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

810
01:00:48,562 --> 01:00:50,481
Chefs who have entered the studio,

811
01:00:50,564 --> 01:00:54,276
please stand behind the sign
with your team name on it.

812
01:00:54,860 --> 01:00:58,614
Filming will begin shortly.
Please take your places.

813
01:00:59,239 --> 01:01:00,949
Once again,

814
01:01:01,033 --> 01:01:03,285
chefs who have entered the studio,

815
01:01:03,369 --> 01:01:06,914
please stand behind the sign
with your team name on it.

816
01:01:07,498 --> 01:01:11,335
Filming will begin shortly.
Please take your places.

817
01:01:39,655 --> 01:01:41,156
We'll begin filming in two minutes.

818
01:01:43,075 --> 01:01:44,159
Studio, stand by.

819
01:01:44,243 --> 01:01:46,787
Filming begins in two minutes.

820
01:01:46,870 --> 01:01:47,913
Everyone, stand by!

821
01:02:54,563 --> 01:02:55,898
I will win at any cost.

822
01:02:56,523 --> 01:02:58,025
I will not lose twice.

823
01:03:07,201 --> 01:03:08,494
Get out of here, Han.

824
01:03:08,577 --> 01:03:10,120
Dad!

825
01:03:10,204 --> 01:03:12,122
Take the stairs and get out of here.

826
01:03:12,206 --> 01:03:13,373
There's no time.

827
01:03:13,457 --> 01:03:15,292
-Get out of here!
-No, Dad!

828
01:03:16,543 --> 01:03:17,544
I'll get help!

829
01:03:17,628 --> 01:03:18,629
Hang in there!

830
01:03:18,712 --> 01:03:20,130
No, Han!

831
01:03:20,714 --> 01:03:23,175
You'll die too if you stay here.

832
01:03:23,258 --> 01:03:24,676
Do as I say.

833
01:03:24,760 --> 01:03:26,094
Listen to me now.

834
01:03:29,515 --> 01:03:30,390
Go now.

835
01:03:33,644 --> 01:03:34,770
Go!

836
01:03:38,148 --> 01:03:39,149
Dad!

837
01:03:39,233 --> 01:03:40,776
Dad!

838
01:03:56,625 --> 01:03:57,501
Dad.

839
01:03:59,378 --> 01:04:00,462
I'll win for you.

840
01:04:02,756 --> 01:04:04,424
The person who got you killed…

841
01:04:05,592 --> 01:04:06,885
I'll beat them for you.

842
01:04:11,139 --> 01:04:11,974
Roll the cameras.

843
01:04:14,101 --> 01:04:15,936
And… cue.

844
01:04:51,597 --> 01:04:54,433
The theme for the first round
of the main competition.

845
01:04:56,018 --> 01:04:56,893
Here it is!

846
01:04:57,853 --> 01:04:59,146
I didn't think it would be this tough.

847
01:04:59,730 --> 01:05:01,732
You have three hours!

848
01:05:01,815 --> 01:05:05,277
I plan to challenge the contestants
in ways they won't expect…

849
01:05:05,360 --> 01:05:08,363
We have to create something
no one's ever seen before.

850
01:05:08,447 --> 01:05:10,032
Do whatever it takes to get it.

851
01:05:10,115 --> 01:05:13,035
What exactly are you
going to do with this?

852
01:05:13,118 --> 01:05:15,078
-Three.
-Let's pick up the pace a bit.

853
01:05:15,162 --> 01:05:17,914
-Two.
-Are you even trying to win?

854
01:05:17,998 --> 01:05:19,082
One.

855
01:05:19,166 --> 01:05:20,876
Please reveal your dish.

856
01:05:21,793 --> 01:05:22,919
We're going to win in style.

857
01:05:29,343 --> 01:05:32,346
Subtitle: Jennifer Jean Lim
